title: A Workers' Congress
card-image: img/cards/peoples_party.svg?v=2
subtitle: Axelrod's old idea of a broad non-party labour congress.
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: party_affairs
view-if: player_party = 'menshevik' and (peoples_party_timer <= 0)
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; peoples_party_timer = 8

Pavel Axelrod has argued since 1905 that Russian workers need a congress of their own, above the parties: unions, cooperatives, mutual aid societies, the lot. Whether it would be a school of democracy or a rival party is the question.

- @call: Call the congress. (1 resource)
- @prepare: Spend the time preparing it, and call it later.
- @easy_discard

@call
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: We have no resources.
on-arrival: {!
RO.pay(Q, 1);
RO.boost(Q, {workers: 5, railway: 4, soldiers: 1});
RO.fac(Q, 'unions', 4, -3);
RO.fac(Q, 'intl', 0, 2);
RO.add(Q, {soviet_democracy: 2});
Q.workers_congress = (Q.workers_congress || 0) + 1;
if (Q.workers_congress >= 2) { RO.boost(Q, {workers: 3}); Q.soviet_democracy += 1; }
!}

Delegates from unions, cooperatives and factory committees met for three days. The Bolsheviks sent delegates and then walked out. It was our best attended meeting in months.

@prepare
on-arrival: {!
RO.fac(Q, 'unions', 2, -2);
Q.peoples_party_timer = 3;
!}

The preparation brought the unions closer to us, and the congress will be easier to call next time.
